  },
  {
   "text": "WORLD\u4e2dhello",
   "v3": 11,
   "v4.7": 18,
   "v4.8": 13
  },
  {
   "text": "Every ``str`` produces a finite token list.",
   "v3": 17,
   "v4.7": 26,
   "v4.8": 21
  },
  {
   "text": "version",
   "v3": 8,
   "v4.7": 12,
   "v4.8": 7
  },
  {
   "text": "text",
   "v3": 8,
   "v4.7": 12,
   "v4.8": 7
  },
  {
   "text": "The list is the frame as \u27e8pad\u27e9 tokens followed by the content tokens, which concatenate back\n    to the marked stream. How many pieces the content takes is family-specific.",
   "v3": 51,
   "v4.7": 70,
   "v4.8": 65
  },
  {
   "text": "text,expected",
   "v3": 10,
   "v4.7": 15,
   "v4.8": 10
  },
  {
   "text": "text,stream,content",
   "v3": 12,
   "v4.7": 17,
   "v4.8": 12
  },
  {
   "text": "Keep the implementation's BMP Mark split aligned with Unicode ``Alphabetic``.",
   "v3": 24,
   "v4.7": 44,
   "v4.8": 39
  },
  {
   "text": "U+0897 is unassigned in Python 3.13's Unicode data but a Mark to ``regex``.",
   "v3": 33,
   "v4.7": 46,
   "v4.8": 41
  },
  {
   "text": "No accent but U+0301 is a piece; the two rows differ only by what the host letters\n    cost, and the mark spelling is one rule with no per-host exception.",
   "v3": 47,
   "v4.7": 62,
   "v4.8": 57
  },
  {
   "text": "\u27e8shift\u27e9 and \u27e8caps\u27e9 both go when an unattached mark run heads the word: `x \u0363The x` reads one\n    over with \u27e8shift\u27e9 written, and v3's `x \u0363HELLO x` reads two under with \u27e8caps\u27e9.",
   "v3": 93,
   "v4.7": 105,
   "v4.8": 99
  },
  {
   "text": "Claude composes Thai SARA AM without applying NFKC generally.",
   "v3": 23,
   "v4.7": 34,
   "v4.8": 29
  },
  {
   "text": "Input noncharacters must not become the engine's structural markers.",
   "v3": 20,
   "v4.7": 30,
   "v4.8": 25
  },
  {
   "text": "version, overhead",
   "v3": 10,
   "v4.7": 16,
   "v4.8": 11
  },
  {
   "text": "literal",
   "v3": 8,
   "v4.7": 13,
   "v4.8": 8
  },
  {
   "text": "The source models know two cased letters newer than Python 3.13's Unicode table.",
   "v3": 26,
   "v4.7": 36,
   "v4.8": 31
  },
  {
   "text": "\u0130 is literal inside a cased span. It does not become a two-byte fallback after an uppercase\n    vocabulary tile; that retired reading over-counted every short form where it still applied.",
   "v3": 49,
   "v4.7": 69,
   "v4.8": 64
  },
  {
   "text": "A float cannot distinguish \"4.1\" from \"4.10\", so versions are not coerced.",
   "v3": 30,
   "v4.7": 40,
   "v4.8": 35
  },
  {
   "text": "v4.8+ reads v4.7's pieces with six frame tokens and no frame \u27e8bow\u27e9.",
   "v3": 35,
   "v4.7": 48,
   "v4.8": 43
  },
  {
   "text": "Below 3.0 is not reconstructed, and neither is a nonsense version string.",
   "v3": 27,
   "v4.7": 38,
   "v4.8": 33
  },
  {
   "text": "bad",
   "v3": 8,
   "v4.7": 13,
   "v4.8": 8
  },
  {
   "text": "The frame's final \u27e8bow\u27e9 is a single leading space; two or more are a whitespace-run token.",
   "v3": 37,
   "v4.7": 46,
   "v4.8": 41
  },
  {
   "text": "version, expected",
   "v3": 10,
   "v4.7": 15,
   "v4.8": 10
  },
